3.The general objects for which the Corporation isconstituted are hereby declared to be—

(a)to take necessary action for the extension andprotection of Buddhism;

(b)to assist in the establishment of Dhamma schools,to establish and conduct of centres for this purpose;

(c)to take action for the conservation and theprotection of social values;

(d)to establish institutions which are actively involvedin eradication social unrest;

(e)to formulate systematic and effective programmesfor eradicating poverty;

(f)to organize activites for the social welfare anddevelopment, using physical resources andknowledge which are inherent to Sri Lanka;

(g)to promote mutual understanding and co-operationas social and national level in the human society;

(h)to plan and implement community welfare,educational and social development projects inSri Lanka;

(i)to promote education, health, recreation, cultureand agriculture, to provide grants, scholarships,gifts, donations and financial assistance for theimprovement, extension and publicize knowledgeand to establish institutions for this purpose;

(j)to promote areas relating to traditional knowledgeand establish institutions for this purpose;

(k)to commence and maintain projects for theprotection and conservation of the environment;

